# VOXELIZE.CanvasBox Dimension Mapping

`CanvasBox` constructor parameters map to local axes **counterintuitively**:

| Parameter | Actual Local Axis |
| --------- | ----------------- |
| `width`   | Z (depth/length)  |
| `height`  | Y (vertical)      |
| `depth`   | X (thickness)     |

authored from intuition, the box comes out rotated a quarter turn about Y and every face painter lands on the wrong side — which reads as a broken texture rather than as swapped dimensions, so it gets debugged in the painter for a while first.

## Example

a fish body that is thin on X (side to side), medium on Y, long on Z (front to back):

```typescript
new VOXELIZE.CanvasBox({
  width: 0.3, // maps to Z (length)
  height: 0.14, // maps to Y (height)
  depth: 0.06, // maps to X (thickness)
});
```

## Face painting

face names (`px`, `nx`, `py`, `ny`, `pz`, `nz`) refer to the **actual** local axes after the swap:

- `px`/`nx`: left/right sides (perpendicular to X)
- `py`/`ny`: top/bottom (perpendicular to Y)
- `pz`/`nz`: front/back (perpendicular to Z)
